## Loop

`Loop` repeats the commands up to its `EndLoop`, as many times as you give it. `Loop(0)` repeats forever, so give it a `Wait` or something else that takes time, and a way out with `BreakLoop`. This loop waits until the player is past the point where X is 100:

```c
Loop(0)
    Call(GetPlayerPos, LVar0, LVar1, LVar2)
    IfGt(LVar0, 100)
        BreakLoop
    EndIf
    Wait(1)
EndLoop
```

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Loop(TIMES)` | Repeats the commands up to `EndLoop` a number of times. `Loop(0)` repeats until something leaves the loop. |
| `EndLoop` | Ends the loop. |
| `BreakLoop` | Leaves the innermost loop. |
| `ContinueLoop` | Skips to the next repeat of the innermost loop. |
| `RetryLoop` | Starts the current repeat of the innermost loop again, without counting it. |

An EVT script can have up to 8 `Loop` and `Lerp` blocks active at once.

## Lerp

`Lerp` moves a variable from one value to another over a number of frames, running its commands once a frame with the new value. Use it to animate something, such as fading in an NPC:

```c
Lerp(LVar0, 0, 255, 30, EASING_LINEAR)
    Call(SetNpcImgFXParams, NPC_SELF, IMGFX_SET_ALPHA, LVar0, 0, 0, 0)
EndLerp
```

`EASING` sets how the value speeds up and slows down, such as `EASING_LINEAR` or `EASING_QUADRATIC_OUT`. `START` and `END` can be whole or decimal numbers.

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Lerp(VAR, START, END, FRAMES, EASING)` | Repeats once a frame, setting `VAR` to a value moving from `START` to `END`. |
| `EndLerp` | Ends a `Lerp`, and waits a frame before the next repeat. |

The commands run for each frame from 0 to `FRAMES`, so you don't need a `Wait`. `BreakLoop` leaves a `Lerp` early, but `ContinueLoop` and `RetryLoop` can't be used inside one, and one `Lerp` can't be inside another.
